Qwen-Image 2.1 reference implementations (architecture only, no code copied)
  tfimage/qwen_image21.py is an independent implementation of the Qwen-Image 2.1 DiT, checked numerically against
  ComfyUI's (https://github.com/comfyanonymous/ComfyUI, comfy/ldm/qwen_image21/model.py, GPL-3.0), which credits
  Hugging Face diffusers (Apache-2.0). The model's math follows those implementations as a specification: the
  block-causal text / reference prefix, t = 0 modulation of prefix tokens, the 3-axis RoPE ids (including the
  half-token centring of reference latents on the target) and the timestep rounding. No source file of ComfyUI or
  diffusers is included.

ComfyUI (host, not included)
  The node in comfyui/ runs inside a user's ComfyUI (GPL-3.0) and imports its modules at run time
  (comfy.model_detection, comfy.model_patcher, comfy.model_management, folder_paths). bench/ drives ComfyUI and
  ComfyUI-GGUF (https://github.com/city96/ComfyUI-GGUF, Apache-2.0) to measure the baseline. Neither is included.

GGUF format (ggml)
  tfimage/gguf_load.py decodes Q8_0, Q4_K, Q5_K and Q6_K blocks on the GPU following ggml's published block
  layouts (https://github.com/ggml-org/ggml, MIT License); reading uses the gguf Python package (MIT), installed
  with pip. The decoders are this project's own and are checked bit-exact against gguf-py.

Quality metrics (downloaded at run time by bench/quality.py, not included)
  lpips (BSD-2-Clause, https://github.com/richzhang/PerceptualSimilarity) and DINOv2 ViT-S/14
  (https://github.com/facebookresearch/dinov2, Apache-2.0) through torch.hub.

scripts/check-public.sh
  From the author's glm53-tensorfold-spark repository (https://github.com/jayleaton/glm53-tensorfold-spark),
  Apache-2.0, same author.

Not included; each user downloads these under their own terms:

Qwen-Image 2.1 weights (diffusion model, Qwen3-VL 8B text encoder, VAE)
  Published by the Qwen team; ComfyUI repackaging at https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1. A GGUF of the
  diffusion model (the results here use a Q6_K one) is made with ComfyUI-GGUF's tools or downloaded from a
  community conversion. See each model card for the license. The images in docs/assets were generated with these
  weights from the prompts in bench/jobs_gate.json.
